```

The function appends a zero byte before computing CRC. The comment says "per RFC 8724" but:
1. The RFC reference is not specific (no section number)
2. This behavior differs from standard CRC-32/ISO-HDLC implementations
3. Callers may not expect the zero-padding

## API Risk
If a user tries to verify RCS using a standard CRC-32 tool, they will get different results. This could cause debugging confusion or interoperability issues with other SCHC implementations.

## Suggested Fix
1. Add RFC section reference to documentation
2. Add a test vector from the RFC or reference implementation
3. Consider offering both padded and unpadded variants if there is ambiguity
